 # Toolbar
 
-The toolbar sits at the top-left of the map. Drag it by the **⋯** handle and collapse it with the hamburger toggle. The language picker is in **Settings**. Each control persists its state to `localStorage` (see [LocalStorage Schema](LocalStorage-Schema)).
-
-![The toolbar collapsed to its hamburger on a phone](img/07-toolbar-collapsed.jpg)
+On a computer the toolbar is a menu bar pinned along the top of the map (the gist's `featureMenubarDrag` lets it be dragged by a **⋯** handle). On a phone or a tablet the same menu is the bottom deck's **Menu** sheet — see [Phone Layout](Phone-Layout). An iPad can be given the menu bar instead with the gist's `featureTabletDesktop`. The language picker is in **Settings**. Each control persists its state to `localStorage` (see [LocalStorage Schema](LocalStorage-Schema)).
 
 ## Section layout
 
@@ -29,18 +27,10 @@ Each header is a full-height row (52 px on a phone): a drawn icon, the title, a
 The **Simulator** is a small ✈ icon in the toolbar footer (next to Terms /
 Privacy) that opens the [Simulator](Simulator-Connect) panel.
 
-### On a phone: the head stays put
-
-The ☰ is the only way in and out of the menus on a phone, and it used to scroll away with
-them — open Display, scroll to the bottom of a long section, and the control that closes it
-is above the top of the screen. The head row (grip, ☰, language) is now pinned to the top of
-the panel while the sections scroll underneath, and it is the **same row the closed card
-shows**, so opening the menu does not rearrange its own head.
+### On a phone or a tablet
 
-**Tapping the map closes the menu.** On a phone the open column covers half the chart, so a
-tap on the map dismisses it — both the open section and the whole column collapse back to the
-☰. Any map interaction counts, so starting a pan or dropping a waypoint clears the menu out of
-the way too.
+The deck's **Menu** button opens the menu as a sheet; its grip and its X close it, and so
+does pressing Menu again. **Tapping the map closes an open section.**
 
